#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064102 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "724bdf2f-c9f0-564e-ae33-c64d44c582ef" :knowledge-point/title "Splitting a Rational Expression With Two Terms in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "6e148f32-5352-5368-a08a-6da278a6068d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5124" :question/problem "Given that $\\dfrac{6y - 1}{3} = ay + b$, what are the values of $a$ and $b$?" :question/worked-solution "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{6y - 1}{3} &= \\ \\dfrac{6y}{3} - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\ \\dfrac{6}{3} \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 \\\\ &= 2 \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 \\\\ &= 2y - \\dfrac 1 3 &. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $ay+b$, we get\n\n$$\n(2)_(⏟)_(a)y + (-\\frac{1}{3})_(⏟)_(b)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and\n\n$$\nb=-\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064103 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0649943a-643f-592f-8815-45c871f7e7dd" :knowledge-point/title "Splitting a Rational Expression With Three Terms in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "41294f0b-dc6a-5a84-a7f8-7c2370b5733c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5125" :question/problem "Given that $\\dfrac{1 - 2a + 16b}{4} = p + qa + rb$, what are the values of $p$, $q$, and $r$?" :question/worked-solution "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{1 - 2a + 16b}{4} &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {2a} {4} + \\dfrac {16b}{4} &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {2} {4} \\cdot a + \\dfrac {16}{4} \\cdot b &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {1} {2} \\cdot a + 4 \\cdot b &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {a} {2} + 4b &= \\ \\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{1}{2}a + 4b &. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $p+qa+rb$, we get\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{4})_(⏟)_(p) + (-\\frac{1}{2})_(⏟)_(q)a + (4)_(⏟)_(r)b\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\np=\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\n$$\nq=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand $r=4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0649943a-643f-592f-8815-45c871f7e7dd" :knowledge-point/title "Splitting a Rational Expression With Three Terms in the Numerator"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76575948-5aa9-591f-9ed4-b205ffc76bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-2594" :question/problem "$\\frac{6a-7b+10}{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6a-7b+10}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{6a}{2}-\\frac{7b}{2}+\\frac{10}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{2}\\cdot a-\\frac{7b}{2}+\\frac{10}{2} & = \\\\ 3a-\\frac{7b}{2}+5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
